COUNSEL REVIEW NOTICE
---------------------
This file defines the intellectual-property license and transfer terms delivered
with the VoxDesk Voice AI Platform repository (`voxdesk-call`). The repository
owner ("Seller") and acquiring party ("Buyer") may elect either:
  (Option A) Exclusive Intellectual Property Assignment upon closing of an Asset
             Purchase Agreement (APA), or
  (Option B) Perpetual, Worldwide, Royalty-Free Commercial Source License.
Both parties should have qualified legal counsel review and countersign the
applicable election in Schedule A prior to closing.

1. GRANT OF RIGHTS (DEFAULT COMMERCIAL SOURCE LICENSE)
------------------------------------------------------
Subject to payment in full of the agreed purchase price under the executed Asset
Purchase Agreement or Marketplace Order ("Closing"), Licensor hereby grants to
Buyer a perpetual, irrevocable (upon payment), worldwide, non-exclusive (unless
Option A Exclusive Assignment is elected in Schedule A), royalty-free license to:
  (a) use, reproduce, modify, prepare derivative works of, compile, and execute
      the Software in source code and object code form;
  (b) deploy, host, and operate the Software on unlimited servers, clusters,
      environments, and customer tenants for internal business operations or
      commercial Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) offerings; and
  (c) sublicense the Software in object/hosted form to Buyer's end-user customers
      and sub-tenants.

2. EXCLUSIVE IP ASSIGNMENT OPTION (BAND C / APA CLOSING)
--------------------------------------------------------
Where Buyer and Seller execute an Exclusive Asset Purchase Agreement referencing
this repository and its due-diligence pack (`dist/due-diligence-<date>.zip`),
all right, title, and interest in and to the proprietary first-party source code,
database schemas, Alembic migrations, documentation, and test suites authored for
VoxDesk transfer to Buyer at Closing, subject only to the open-source licenses of
third-party dependencies enumerated in `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md` and `sbom/`.

3. THIRD-PARTY OPEN-SOURCE COMPONENTS & SYNTHESIZED ASSETS
----------------------------------------------------------
This repository links against third-party open-source packages (Python, Node.js,
Go, Rust) governed by their respective permissive licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0,
BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, MPL-2.0) as inventoried in
`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md` and the CycloneDX SBOMs under `sbom/`.
Bundled ambient background audio WAV files (`app/assets/ambient/*.wav`) are
deterministically synthesized 16-bit 8 kHz mono PCM waveforms generated by
VoxDesk (`CC0-1.0` / Public Domain equivalent) with zero third-party copyrighted
recordings.

